{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2766 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1245c65320ea1042ccbbb8c3aab9c0d3c0a283c9a95e5f82f25cfc54ab8e6faa" :edb/db-before-t 2765 :edb/db-after-t 2766 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536078 50 #inst "2026-10-09T14:30:04.956Z" 13194139536078 true] [17592186217191 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382595 13194139536078 true] [17592186217191 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382602 13194139536078 true] [17592186217192 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382609 13194139536078 true] [17592186217192 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382616 13194139536078 true] [17592186217742 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536078 true] [17592186217742 1100 "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+4({y}^{′})^{2}-{y}^{′}.\n$$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186217742 1100 "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$y = xy^{′} + 4(y^{′})^{2} - y^{′}$." 13194139536078 false] [17592186217742 1145 "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+4({y}^{′})^{2}-{y}^{′},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+4{p}^{2}-p.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+4{p}^{2}-p)^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+8p{p}^{′}-{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+8p-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+4{p}^{2}-p,$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+4{c}^{2}-c.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382595 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382596 13194139536078 true] [17592186382595 1089 "q-334203" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382595 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536078 true] [17592186382595 1100 "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+({y}^{′})^{3}-2{y}^{′}.\n$$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382595 1113 #uuid "284f78d5-711d-538b-9fce-2df62ab28f45" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382595 1145 "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+({y}^{′})^{3}-2{y}^{′},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+{p}^{3}-2p.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+{p}^{3}-2p)^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+3{p}^{2}{p}^{′}-2{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+3{p}^{2}-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+{p}^{3}-2p,$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+{c}^{3}-2c.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382597 13194139536078 true] [17592186382596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382598 13194139536078 true] [17592186382596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382599 13194139536078 true] [17592186382596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382600 13194139536078 true] [17592186382596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382601 13194139536078 true] [17592186382596 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536078 true] [17592186382596 1041 "selection" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382596 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382599 13194139536078 true] [17592186382596 1110 #uuid "7d67aab9-73af-5fc9-afac-f2cb1374dbea" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382597 1034 "y={c}^{2}x+{c}^{3}-2c" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382597 1111 #uuid "b4327a05-2572-52ce-b7a3-1c7e8e4e8354" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382598 1034 "y={c}^{3}x+{c}^{3}-2c" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382598 1111 #uuid "1258649e-a167-5438-a5ce-53173eb41888" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382599 1034 "y=cx+{c}^{3}-2c" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382599 1111 #uuid "f0b66cc4-7f78-5e90-bcfd-5f782b836a8b" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382600 1034 "y=cx+2{c}^{3}-2c" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382600 1111 #uuid "654a8f27-f4f5-5530-a010-d1511f035c33" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382601 1034 "y=cx+{c}^{2}-2c" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382601 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382601 1111 #uuid "019b0c8a-6b1b-520f-aff7-84c20fe95c36" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382602 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382603 13194139536078 true] [17592186382602 1089 "q-334210" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382602 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536078 true] [17592186382602 1100 "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}},\\,{y}^{′}\\ne 0.\n$$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382602 1113 #uuid "796e83ce-3077-5464-bc5e-9be0563f9d98" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382602 1145 "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+\\frac{1}{p}.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={(xp+\\frac{1}{p})}^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-\\frac{1}{{p}^{2}}{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-\\frac{1}{{p}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c,\n$$\n\nwith the restriction $c\\ne 0.$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+\\frac{1}{p},$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+\\frac{1}{c}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c\\ne 0.$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382604 13194139536078 true] [17592186382603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382605 13194139536078 true] [17592186382603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382606 13194139536078 true] [17592186382603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382607 13194139536078 true] [17592186382603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382608 13194139536078 true] [17592186382603 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536078 true] [17592186382603 1041 "selection" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382603 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382607 13194139536078 true] [17592186382603 1110 #uuid "7efd41de-7ae6-5e88-8a98-2eda4a55bc39" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382604 1034 "y=cx+c" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382604 1111 #uuid "b13115f3-906f-5193-99bb-1a1901e0d883" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382605 1034 "y=cx+\\frac{1}{2c}" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382605 1111 #uuid "89034d07-4829-5254-a3b9-249d0be9bea8" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382606 1034 "y={c}^{2}x+\\frac{1}{c}" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382606 1111 #uuid "9b625242-479c-5943-9a7f-a03b4d67a566" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382607 1034 "y=cx+\\frac{1}{c}" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382607 1111 #uuid "9ea004f6-60a3-513e-83dc-66736662fe04" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382608 1034 "y={c}^{3}x+\\frac{1}{c}" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382608 1111 #uuid "a0fc36dd-a482-549c-8fbc-83098f16eb1b" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382609 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382610 13194139536078 true] [17592186382609 1089 "q-334453" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382609 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536078 true] [17592186382609 1100 "Find the singular solution to the following Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{{y}^{′}},\\,{y}^{′}\\ge 0.\n$$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382609 1113 #uuid "19fc08b5-a70b-5aaf-9e22-7a42cd64e91f" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382609 1145 "A Clairaut differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $g$ is a differentiable function of ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTo solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+\\sqrt{p}.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+\\sqrt{p})^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}}{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, so at least one factor must be zero.\n\nThe singular solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if $x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}}=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute this into $y=xp+\\sqrt{p}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =xp+\\sqrt{p} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}})p+\\sqrt{p} \\\\  & =-\\frac{p}{2\\sqrt{p}}+\\sqrt{p} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the singular solution is given parametrically by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}} \\\\ y=\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo eliminate $p,$ we first solve the first equation for $\\sqrt{p}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{p}=-\\frac{1}{2x}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}},$ we must have $x<0.$\n\nNext, let's substitute this expression for $\\sqrt{p}$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{2x})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the explicit form of the singular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{4x},\\,x<0.\n$$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382611 13194139536078 true] [17592186382610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382612 13194139536078 true] [17592186382610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382613 13194139536078 true] [17592186382610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382614 13194139536078 true] [17592186382610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382615 13194139536078 true] [17592186382610 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536078 true] [17592186382610 1041 "selection" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382610 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382611 13194139536078 true] [17592186382610 1110 #uuid "d95d9587-c73a-57a9-9174-9e73c054a9e5" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382611 1034 "y=-\\frac{1}{4x},\\,x<0" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382611 1111 #uuid "cc15b468-9835-5cc4-9215-8542fefe13dc" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382612 1034 "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\,x<0" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382612 1111 #uuid "ce158720-1fc7-527b-87d0-908f5cce6c4f" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382613 1034 "y=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,x<0" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382613 1111 #uuid "922361bf-f167-5db2-a557-55ff20814d20" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382614 1034 "y=-\\frac{1}{2x},\\,x<0" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382614 1111 #uuid "d08d2f5c-20e6-5fc4-8cdb-ff66476287ec" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382615 1034 "y=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,x>0" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382615 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382615 1111 #uuid "5aa110e4-0af4-5d43-9f6d-7aeda212de3b" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382616 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382617 13194139536078 true] [17592186382616 1089 "q-334457" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382616 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536078 true] [17592186382616 1100 "Find the singular solution to the following Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′}),\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le {y}^{′}\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382616 1113 #uuid "433e97c3-88c2-5dfc-9c81-2ab81a0cbb54" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382616 1145 "A Clairaut differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $g$ is a differentiable function of ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTo solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p).\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p))^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p){p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, so at least one factor must be zero.\n\nThe singular solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if $x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p).\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute this into $y=xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p))p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p) \\\\  & =p\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the singular solution is given parametrically by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p) \\\\ y=p\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo eliminate $p,$ we first solve the first equation for $p:$\n\n$$\np=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nThis is valid only for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le p\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nNext, let's substitute this expression for $p$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =p\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)\\cdot x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the explicit form of the singular solution is\n\n$$\ny=x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1.\n$$" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382618 13194139536078 true] [17592186382617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382619 13194139536078 true] [17592186382617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382620 13194139536078 true] [17592186382617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382621 13194139536078 true] [17592186382617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382622 13194139536078 true] [17592186382617 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536078 true] [17592186382617 1041 "selection" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382617 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382621 13194139536078 true] [17592186382617 1110 #uuid "5b84fb95-2319-5db5-bf51-b8e12537dc88" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382618 1034 "y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382618 1111 #uuid "424bbb5c-ce45-5484-ae8a-0478fc3620bb" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382619 1034 "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382619 1111 #uuid "0030d570-af4b-5827-8618-b37e058d369b" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382620 1034 "y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382620 1111 #uuid "ca74d12f-cf40-58d9-b177-25f3b72dc052" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382621 1034 "y=x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1" 13194139536078 true] [17592186382621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536078 true] [17592186382621 1111 #uuid "e48d63ef-c40b-5f1d-ab43-32f57ab8213d" 13194139536078 true] [175921